From 683459767c14db88c8192b15125f05e1ff6ba665 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MOTOR-44 (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:44:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] branding: FlyWeb fly as the NTP and version page favicons

Chromium 156 shows its own logos on two internal pages that Brave's
resource overrides do not cover:
- IDR_NTP_FAVICON (common/favicon_ntp.png, a grey Chrome logo): the new
  tab page, also used by What's New and contextual tasks;
- IDR_PRODUCT_FAVICON (components/resources/*/chromium/favicon_product.png,
  the Chromium logo): chrome://version.
Add both, copied from the FlyWeb tab logo (product_logo_16.png, from M2),
so updateBranding copies them over Chromium's.

The NTP favicon is themified by Chromium because its own icon is a glyph;
ThemeFavicon() would mask the colored fly into a silhouette on light tabs
(contrast 2.2-2.9 against the 3.0 threshold). Skip it for the NTP hosts,
as Brave already does for the welcome page. chrome://version is not
themified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
